  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Abhijeet Suresh Kurle And Anr vs The State Of Maharashtra on 10 November, 2022 Author: R. N. Laddha Bench: Revati Mohite Dere, R. N. Laddha bipin prithiani 1 Digitally signed by Bipin In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bipin Dharmender Dharmender Prithiani Prithiani Date: 2022.11.11 Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction 18:26:10 +0530 Criminal Writ Petition No. 4245 Of 2021 Abhijeet Suresh Kurle & Anr. ... Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Mr. Ashok P. Mundargi, Senior Advocate i/by Mr. Chetan Ms. Rama Somani for the Petitioners. Ms. S. D. Shinde, App for the Respondent-State. Coram: Revati Mohite Dere R. N. Laddha, Jj.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Learned senior counsel for the petitioners submits that the complaint/FIR itself is not maintainable in as much as the complaint/FIR is lodged by the Police Hawaldar and the same is in contravention of the Section 42 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, in particular Section 42(5). He further submits that even Section 188 of the Indian Penal Code is not applicable having regard to the period when the notification was in force.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned senior counsel for the petitioners submits that the complaint/FIR itself is not maintainable in as much as the complaint/FIR is lodged by the Police Hawaldar and the same is in contravention of the Section 42 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, in particular Section 42(5). He further submits that even Section 188 of the Indian Penal Code is not applicable having regard to the period when the notification was in force.",
